injection context, which produces NG0203, and the bundle carries Angular twice.

499
00:30:37,659 --> 00:30:41,933
VER-003 · Report 1: Angular as a regular dependency

500
00:30:43,058 --> 00:30:46,511
Frameworks and any package whose instance must be

501
00:30:46,511 --> 00:30:49,965
shared (Angular, the CDK, RxJS) belong in peerDependencies.

502
00:30:49,965 --> 00:30:54,281
The application installs exactly one copy, and the package manager

503
00:30:54,281 --> 00:30:58,598
reports a conflict instead of silently duplicating it. tslib stays

504
00:30:58,598 --> 00:31:02,483
in dependencies (it is what ng-packagr's own template does).

505
00:31:03,859 --> 00:31:07,907
VER-003 · Report 2: one entry point for everything

506
00:31:09,032 --> 00:31:11,976
With a single entry point, every consumer depends

507
00:31:11,976 --> 00:31:14,920
on every component's dependencies, types and module-level code.

508
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:17,863
The button's users pay for the date picker.

509
00:31:19,239 --> 00:31:23,469
VER-003 · Report 2: one entry point for everything

510
00:31:24,594 --> 00:31:30,162
Fix: secondary entry points, one per component family: @acme/ui/button, @acme/ui/select,

511
00:31:30,162 --> 00:31:35,731
@acme/ui/date-picker. ng-packagr builds each one separately, and only the date

512
00:31:35,731 --> 00:31:40,744
picker imports date-fns, which becomes an optional peer dependency.

513
00:31:42,119 --> 00:31:46,039
VER-003 · Report 3: export made internals public

514
00:31:47,164 --> 00:31:51,075
export from internal/dom-utils published every function in that file.

515
00:31:51,075 --> 00:31:55,856
Whatever the folder name says, a symbol importable from the package

516
00:31:55,856 --> 00:32:00,637
is public API (see VER-001), and removing it was a breaking

517
00:32:00,637 --> 00:32:04,984
change in a minor release. select-option-row.component has the same problem.

518
00:32:06,359 --> 00:32:10,412
VER-003 · Report 3: export made internals public

519
00:32:11,537 --> 00:32:14,828
Fix: explicit, named exports from each entry point,

520
00:32:14,828 --> 00:32:19,766
so publishing something is a deliberate act, plus an API report (golden

521
00:32:19,766 --> 00:32:24,703
file) checked in CI so any change to the public surface is

522
00:32:24,703 --> 00:32:25,937
visible in review.

523
00:32:25,937 --> 00:32:31,286
Share internal code between entry points through a dedicated internal entry point (for

524
00:32:31,286 --> 00:32:36,224
example @acme/ui/internal) documented as having no compatibility guarantees, or keep it unexported.

