565
00:35:05,274 --> 00:35:09,484
Apologise in the release notes; it was a breaking change in a minor.

566
00:35:10,859 --> 00:35:12,969
VER-003 · Follow-up 1

567
00:35:14,094 --> 00:35:17,743
Which Angular versions should @acme/ui 5.x declare in its

568
00:35:17,743 --> 00:35:21,393
peer range, and how would you test that claim?

569
00:35:26,651 --> 00:35:29,816
Declare only the framework versions actually supported and tested.

570
00:35:29,816 --> 00:35:34,037
Build a consumer matrix at the minimum and relevant releases within the

571
00:35:34,037 --> 00:35:38,258
range, including forms, secondary entry points, harnesses, and zoneless behavior where supported.

572
00:35:38,258 --> 00:35:41,775
A broad greater-than-or-equal range claims future compatibility you cannot validate.

573
00:35:41,775 --> 00:35:46,348
Use bounded compatible ranges when appropriate and revise them as releases are tested.

574
00:35:46,348 --> 00:35:49,161
Do not choose the range solely from the

575
00:35:49,161 --> 00:35:51,623
framework version installed in the library workspace.

576
00:35:52,998 --> 00:35:55,232
VER-003 · Follow-up 2

577
00:35:56,358 --> 00:36:02,922
How would you migrate consumers from @acme/ui to @acme/ui/button imports automatically?

578
00:36:08,219 --> 00:36:11,570
Resolve named imports from the root entry point and

579
00:36:11,570 --> 00:36:14,550
map supported symbols to their feature entry points.

580
00:36:14,550 --> 00:36:17,529
Split mixed imports where needed, preserve type-only imports

581
00:36:17,529 --> 00:36:20,136
and aliases, and update tests and documentation.

582
00:36:20,136 --> 00:36:22,370
Report ambiguous wildcard or dynamic imports.

583
00:36:22,370 --> 00:36:26,467
Validate the result against the packed package, not monorepo path mappings.

584
00:36:26,467 --> 00:36:29,819
Keep a root compatibility re-export during a deprecation window

585
00:36:29,819 --> 00:36:33,171
when feasible, then remove it in the announced major.

586
00:36:34,546 --> 00:36:36,799
VER-003 · Follow-up 3

587
00:36:37,924 --> 00:36:43,294
What does a consumer see when two of their dependencies need incompatible peer ranges?

588
00:36:48,701 --> 00:36:52,079
The package manager may report a peer conflict or

589
00:36:52,079 --> 00:36:55,083
refuse installation depending on its version and policy.

590
00:36:55,083 --> 00:36:58,461
Forcing installation can produce a graph outside one library's

591
00:36:58,461 --> 00:37:01,465
supported range, leading to build or runtime failures.

592
00:37:01,465 --> 00:37:03,717
Align dependency versions, upgrade a library,

593
00:37:03,717 --> 00:37:06,721
or use supported alternatives rather than ignoring the

594
00:37:06,721 --> 00:37:07,471
conflict automatically.

595
00:37:07,471 --> 00:37:10,850
Inspect the resolved graph and test the resulting consumer.

596
00:37:10,850 --> 00:37:15,731
Peer metadata communicates a constraint; it does not prove runtime compatibility by itself.

597
00:37:17,106 --> 00:37:19,225
Implementation clarification · Direct-reference compatibility

598
00:37:20,350 --> 00:37:25,011
The deprecation correction changes kind() from primary to undefined when unset.

599
00:37:25,011 --> 00:37:28,401
Consumers reading that getter can observe the change

600
00:37:28,401 --> 00:37:31,368
even though the rendered default stays primary.

601
00:37:31,368 --> 00:37:33,910
Treat those reads as migration cases.

602
00:37:35,286 --> 00:37:37,820
Implementation clarification · Installation versus imports

603
00:37:38,945 --> 00:37:43,770
Secondary entry points alone do not make date-fns optional to install.

604
00:37:43,770 --> 00:37:47,280
Optional peer metadata or a separate package must

605
00:37:47,280 --> 00:37:50,351
match the isolated feature and its declarations.

606
00:37:51,726 --> 00:37:52,894
Final review checklist

607
00:37:54,018 --> 00:37:58,304
Review the lesson by answering each main question and follow-up aloud.

608
00:37:58,304 --> 00:38:01,421
For Versioning Angular Libraries: Compatibility and Safe Migration,

609
00:38:01,421 --> 00:38:04,148
connect each reported symptom to its mechanism,

610
00:38:04,148 --> 00:38:08,044
explain the corrected public contract, and name a regression check

611
00:38:08,044 --> 00:38:09,992
that exercises the consumer path.

612
00:38:09,992 --> 00:38:12,329
State compatibility and accessibility limitations clearly.

613
00:38:12,329 --> 00:38:15,056
The linked transcript, complete code, source questions,

614
00:38:15,056 --> 00:38:18,952
and verification report let you repeat the exercises at your

615
00:38:18,952 --> 00:38:19,732
own pace.

616
00:38:20,773 --> 00:38:23,111
